The reduction of metal oxide to metal by carbon is exothermic under the reaction equation:  
\[ \text{Zn} + \frac{1}{2} \text{O}_2 \rightarrow \text{ZnO} \]  
The heat released is given by:  
\[ \Delta H = -298.5 \text{ kJ/mol} \]  
Thus, the heat released is negative, indicating an exothermic reaction.  
