","Ssorption isotherms are graphical representations of the equilibrium between the concentration of a solute (e.g., an organic contaminant) in a solution and the concentration adsorbed from the solution onto a solid surface (e.g., a natural sorbent). They are used to study the behavior of pollutants, pollutants in the water, or pharmaceuticals in the environment.

