   \[
   \sqrt{x+4} - \sqrt{x} = 1 \implies 1 = \sqrt{x+4} - \sqrt{x}
   \]
   Square both sides:
   \[
   1 = (\sqrt{x+4} - \sqrt{x})^2 = 1 + 2\sqrt{x(x+4)} - x
   \]
   Subtract 1 from both sides:
   \[
   0 = 2\sqrt{x(x+4)} - x
   \]
   Add x to both sides:
   \[
   x = 2\sqrt{x(x+4)}
   \]

