\text{Number of multiples of 3 or 4} = \text{Number of multiples of 3} + \text{Number of multiples of 4} - \text{Number of multiples of both 3 and 4}
\]
\[
= 10 + 7 - 2 = 15
\]
The probability that the number on her card will be a multiple of 3 or 4 is the number of multiples of 3 or 4 divided by the total number of cards, which is 30.
