","To determine if \( n(n+1) \) can be a perfect power for any non-negative integer \( n \), we analyze the properties of \( n(n+1) \). 

1. If \( n = 0 \), \( n(n+1) = 0 \), which is \( 0^2 \), so it is a perfect power.
2. If \( n = 1 \), \( n(n+1) = 1 \), which is \( 1^2 \), so it is a perfect power.
3. If \( n = 3 \), \( n(n+1) = 3 \cdot 4 = 12 \), which is not a perfect power.
