To calculate the average radiation dose to the leadula, we use the formula:  
\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \frac{\text{absorbed dose ( mJ)}}{\text{mass (g)}} \times 10^{-6}
\]  
Given:  
- Absorbed dose = 0.12 J = 120 mJ  
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg = 1600 g  

Substituting the values:  
\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \frac{120 \text{ mJ}}{1600 \text{ g}} \times 10^{-6} = 0.075 \text{ mSv}
\]  
Thus, the average radiation dose to the liver is \(\boxed{0.075 \text{ mSv}}\).
