","To find the magnetic field strength at the center of a circular coil, we can use the formula:

B = (μ₀ * N * I) / (2 * R)

where B is the magnetic field strength, μ₀ is the permeability of free space (4π × 10^(-7) Tm/A), N is the number of turns in the coil, I is the current in the coil, and R is the radius of the coil.

Given the values:
N = 100 turns
I = 1 A
R = 0.2 m

Plugging these values into the formula:

B = (4π × 10^(-7) Tm/A * 100 * 1 A) / (2 * 0.2 m)

B = (4π × 10^(-5) Tm) / 0.4 m

B = 10π × 10^(-5) T

B ≈ 3.1416 × 10^(-4) T

So, the magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is approximately 3.1416 × 10^(-4) T.",relevance,"# Task Description
