   \[
   A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 + m_v} = \frac{100}{1 + 0.1} = \frac{100}{1.1} \approx 90.9 \text{ dB}
   \]

2. **Determine the new voltage gain \( A_{v}' \):**
   The gain falls by 6 dB, so:
   \[
   A_{v}' = A_v \times 10^{-0.06} = 100 \times 10^{-0.06} \approx 94.9 \text{ dB}
   \]

3. **Calculate the new closed-loop gain \( A_{vf}' \):**
   \[
   A_{vf}' = \frac{A_{v}'}{1 + m_v} = \frac{94.9}{1 + 0.1} = \frac{94.9}{1.1} \approx 85.9 \text{ dB}
   \]

4. **Compute the percentage change in the closed-loop gain:**
   \[
   \text{Percentage Change} = \left( \frac{A_{vf}' - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{85.9 - 90.9}{90.9} \right) \times 100 \approx -4.9\%
   \]

   **Final Answer**: The percent change in the closed-loop gain is \(\boxed{-4.9\%}\).
