To find the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of the symmetric matrix \([D] = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \end{bmatrix}\) using the Gram-Jacobi algorithm, we follow these steps:

1. **Compute the eigenvalues and eigenvectors** using Gram-Gram-Gram-Gram-Gram-Geman-Gonon algorithm.
2. **Compute the eigenvalues** using the eigenvalues of the matrix \([D]\).

The eigenvalues of \([D]\) are \(\boxed{1, 2, 3}\). The corresponding eigenvectors are:
\[
\boxed{\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 1 \\ 2 \end{bmatrix}}
\]

Thus, the orthogonal matrix \([R]\) is:
\[
\boxed{\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & 2 \end{bmatrix}}
\]

Thus, the eigenvalues are \(\boxed{1, 2, 3}\), and the eigenvectors are \(\boxed{\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 1 \\ 2 \end{bmatrix}}\).
