v(t) = \frac{1}{C} \int i(t) \, dt = \frac{1}{C} \int 0.2e^{-4t} \, dt = \frac{0}{C} e^{-4t} + \frac{1}{C} C = \frac{0.05}{C} e^{-4t}
\]
However, the given voltage is \( 10e^{-4t} \), so the correct relationship is:
\[
