The uncertainty principle for time and energy is given by:
\[
\Delta E \cdot \Delta t \geq \frac{\hbar}{2}
\]
where \(\hbar\) is the reduced Planck constant (\(\hbar = 1.0 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s} = 5.3 \times 10^{-12} \text{ eV s}\)).

